              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_table_3.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Class interval</td><td>Number of students (f<sub>i</sub>)</td><td>Class mark (x<sub>i</sub>)</td><td>f<sub>i</sub>x<sub>i</sub></td></tr><tr><td>10 - 25</td><td>2</td><td>17.5</td><td>35.0</td></tr><tr><td>25 - 40</td><td>3</td><td>32.5</td><td>97.5</td></tr><tr><td>40 - 55</td><td>7</td><td>47.5</td><td>332.5</td></tr><tr><td>55 - 70</td><td>6</td><td>62.5</td><td>375.0</td></tr><tr><td>70 - 85</td><td>6</td><td>77.5</td><td>465.0</td></tr><tr><td>85 - 100</td><td>6</td><td>92.5</td><td>555.0</td></tr><tr><td>Total</td><td>Σf<sub>i</sub> = 30</td><td></td><td>Σf<sub>i</sub>x<sub>i</sub> = 1860.0</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.386,
            0.9,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sum of the values in the last column gives us "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Sigma f _ { i } x _ { i } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " So, the mean "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\overline { { x } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the given data is given by"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.342,
            0.42,
            0.602,
            0.464
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\overline{x} = \\frac{\\Sigma f_{i}x_{i}}{\\Sigma f_{i}} = \\frac{1860.0}{30} = 62"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.467,
            0.832,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This new method of finding the mean is known as the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Direct Method",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.494,
            0.902,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We observe that Tables 13.1 and 13.3 are using the same data and employing the same formula for the calculation of the mean but the results obtained are different. Can you think why this is so, and which one is more accurate? The difference in the two values is because of the mid-point assumption in Table 13.3, 59.3 being the exact mean, while 62 an approximate mean."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.602,
            0.902,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sometimes when the numerical values of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x _ { i }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f _ { i }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are large, finding the product of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x _ { i }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f _ { i }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " becomes tedious and time consuming. So, for such situations, let us think of a method of reducing these calculations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.669,
            0.902,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can do nothing with the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f _ { i } ^ { \\flat } \\mathrm { { S } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , but we can change each "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x _ { i }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to a smaller number so that our calculations become easy. How do we do this? What about subtracting a fixed number from each of these "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x _ { i } ^ {   ^ { \\prime } } \\mathrm { S }   _ { \\cdot } ^ { \\mathrm { ? } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let us try this method."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.736,
            0.902,
            0.817
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The first step is to choose one among the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x _ { i } ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " s as the assumed mean, and denote it by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } a ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Also, to further reduce our calculation work, we may take "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ \\circ a ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to be that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x _ { i }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " which lies in the centre of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x_{_1},x_{_2},\\ldots,x_{_n}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . So, we can choose "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 4 7 . 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 6 2 . 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Let us choose "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 4 7 . 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.824,
            0.899,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The next step is to find the difference "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "d _ { i }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " between a and each of the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x _ { i } ^ { \\mathrm { ~ \\prime ~ } } \\mathrm { S }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , that is, the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "deviation",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { \\circ } a ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from each of the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x _ { i } ^ { \\mathrm { ~ \\prime ~ } } \\mathrm { S }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.872,
            0.139,
            0.888
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.342,
            0.871,
            0.566,
            0.892
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "d _ { _ i } = x _ { _ i } - a = x _ { _ i } - 4 7 . 5"
        },
